= Using the compiler class =

The [../classes/html/classcompiler.html compiler class] provides a generic compiler framework.

Though targeted at code-to-code translation (transcompiling), it could be used as the basis for any type of translation or compilation system.

Translation/compilation is achieved in three steps:

* Pre-processing - A unit of code is passed through a chain of pre-processing modules.  Pre-processing modules should inherit from the compilerpreprocessor class and implement the process() method.
* Processing - The output of the final pre-processing module is parsed by an instance of the codetree class, producing a DOM tree which represents the code.  The tree is then passed through a chain of processing modules.  Processing modules should inherit from the compilerprocessor class and implement the process() method.
* Post-processing - The output of the processing step is passed through a chain of post-processing modules.  Post-processing modules should inherit from the compilerpostprocessor class and implement the process() method.

Input and output grammars must be set to define the input and output formats.  See the [codetree.html codetree class] for information on the grammar format.

The following example creates simple preprocessor, processor, and postprocessor classes, defines a grammar, sets the input and output grammars, adds the processing modules, and compiles a string.

